    "summary": "Model built and verified for a single simply supported span, 25 m bearing-centre-to-centre, 16 m deck width, Highway Class II loading.\n\nRoot cause of the failure: the accepted decision lane.qk was 10.5 kN/m, the Class I value, instead of the Class II value. Per JTG D60-2015 4.3.1, the lane distributed load for Class II is 10.5 × 0.75 = 7.875 kN/m. Re-proposing lane.qk = 7.875 with evidence [JTGD60-4.3.1-qk, INPUT:deck.load_class] fixed the model.\n\nFinal model:\n- Idealization spine_beam_2d, system simply_supported; 5 precast prestressed small-box girders per span (C40), modelled as an equivalent single beam.\n- Section (integrated): A_single = 1.0605 m2, I_single = 0.2517 m4; combined A = 5.303 m2, I = 1.258 m4.\n- gamma = 26 kN/m3 (JTG D60-2015 4.2.1), w = 137.87 kN/m (girder self-weight only), m = 14.054 t/m.\n- Bearings: plain laminated elastomeric, 2 per girder end × 5 girders = 10 per support line, 300×350 mm, 4×8 mm rubber layers; modelled as vertical + longitudinal springs with free rotation. S = 10.096, Kv = 1.416e7 kN/m, Kh = 3.28e4 kN/m per line.\n- Live load: 4 design lanes, xi = 0.67, qk = 7.875 kN/m, Pk = 232.5 kN, mu = 0.2409 (from f1 = 4.272 Hz, JTG D60-2015 4.3.2).\n\nResults: first vertical frequency 4.272 Hz; self-weight support reactions 1723.35 kN each (sum = 3446.7 kN = 26 × 5.303 × 25, consistent with L3-2); self-weight midspan moment 10770.9 kNm; live-load maximum positive moment 6878.4 kNm. L1/L2/L3 checks all pass."
